#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# number_field_discriminant

#% text
# `number_field_discriminant(a)` gives the discriminant of the number field `Q(a)` generated by the algebraic number `a`: the discriminant of its ring of integers.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The discriminant of the minimal polynomial (made monic and integral) is divided by the square of the index of the order it defines in the ring of integers; the index is found prime by prime, by adding algebraic integers `w` with `p w` in the order until none is left.

#% item
# A rational number gives 1; a list gives the list of discriminants.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
number_field_discriminant(sqrt(2) + sqrt(3))
#% output
#= 2304

#% cell
number_field_discriminant([sqrt(2), 2^(1/3), 2^(1/4)])
#% output
#= [8, -108, -2048]

#% text
# The ring of integers of `Q(sqrt(5))` is larger than `Z[sqrt(5)]`: the discriminant is that of the golden ratio's polynomial:

#% cell
[number_field_discriminant(sqrt(5)), discriminant(x^2 - x - 1, x), discriminant(x^2 - 5, x)]
#% output
#= [5, 5, 20]

#% cell
number_field_discriminant(root(x => x^3 + x + 1, 3))
#% output
#= -31

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `minimal_polynomial`, `discriminant`, `to_number_field`
